 "notes": "Decaying ALP DM two-photon line search with JWST NIRSpec IFU spectroscopy (a->2gamma). Headline combined limit from Fig. 1 ('Our work (combined)', navy solid boundary = lower edge of blue excluded region), extracted from the vector file simple_limit.pdf (drawing idx 52). This is the union/envelope of the three grating datasets (G395, G235, G140) shown separately in Fig. 2. Axis calibration: x-axis log with ticks 0.6/1/2 eV (~952 px/decade); y-axis log 1e-11 to 1e-10 (364 px/decade). Curve spans m_a = 0.47-2.55 eV, strongest g_agamma ~7.4e-12 GeV^-1 near 2.4 eV; small upward spike at ~0.61 eV is a real feature of the traced curve. 95% CL upper limit (Delta chi^2 = 2.71). MW halo NFW profile assumed (rho_s=0.18 GeV/cm^3, r_s=24 kpc); decay flux depends on the line-of-sight D-factor rather than a single local density, so dm_density_assumed left null per convention for these D-factor decay searches.",
